      <title id="bb-evidence-chain-title">The agentic chain from human intent to runtime proof</title>
      <desc id="bb-evidence-chain-desc">A human approves intent. A coding agent uses Blackbox Skills to propose EARS requirements, Gherkin scenarios, an executable flow, runtime configuration, and effect policy. Deterministic Blackbox components run the real system, seal runtime evidence, and compute separate test, integrity, effect, and observable decision coverage verdicts. The agent interprets findings and repairs the implementation.</desc>
